{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ChainLetter"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Persisting Models"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Save and load Markov models for later use."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/chainletter\/persistingmodels"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Building a Markov model from a large corpus can take time. ChainLetter supports full ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance, allowing you to save trained models to disk and reload them instantly.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Saving-a-Model","type":"heading","text":"Saving a Model","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"JSONEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to serialize a model:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import ChainLetter","import Foundation","","\/\/ Train the model","let model = MarkovText(largeCorpus)","","\/\/ Encode to JSON","let encoder = JSONEncoder()","encoder.outputFormatting = .prettyPrinted  \/\/ Optional: human-readable","let data = try encoder.encode(model)","","\/\/ Write to disk","let url = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"model.json\")","try data.write(to: url)"]},{"anchor":"Loading-a-Model","type":"heading","text":"Loading a Model","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"JSONDecoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to restore a saved model:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let url = URL(fileURLWithPath: \"model.json\")","let data = try Data(contentsOf: url)","","let decoder = JSONDecoder()","var model = try decoder.decode(MarkovText.self, from: data)","","\/\/ Optional: compile for faster generation","model.compile()","","\/\/ Ready to use","if let sentence = model.makeSentence() {","    print(sentence)","}"]},{"anchor":"What-Gets-Saved","type":"heading","text":"What Gets Saved","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following data is persisted:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Property","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Description","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"stateSize","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The N-gram size","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"chain.model","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All state transitions with counts","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"parsedSentences","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Original corpus for overlap checking (if ","type":"text"},{"code":"retainOriginal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" was true)","type":"text"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"anchor":"What-Doesnt-Get-Saved","type":"heading","text":"What Doesn’t Get Saved","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"text":" persisted:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Property","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"compiled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Recompute with ","type":"text"},{"code":"compile()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after loading","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom closures","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sentence\/word splitters reset to defaults","type":"text"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"anchor":"Restoring-Custom-Closures","type":"heading","text":"Restoring Custom Closures","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you used custom splitters, you’ll need to reapply them after loading:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Original model with custom splitter","let original = MarkovText(","    corpus,","    sentenceSplitter: myCustomSplitter",")","","\/\/ After loading, the model uses default splitters","var loaded = try decoder.decode(MarkovText.self, from: data)","","\/\/ For generation, this usually doesn't matter since the model","\/\/ is already built. But if you need the same behavior, create","\/\/ a new model with the loaded chain:","let restored = MarkovText(","    chain: loaded.chain,","    parsedSentences: nil  \/\/ Already in the chain",")"]},{"anchor":"Binary-Encoding","type":"heading","text":"Binary Encoding","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For smaller file sizes, use a binary encoder like ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyListEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Save as binary plist","let encoder = PropertyListEncoder()","encoder.outputFormat = .binary","let data = try encoder.encode(model)","try data.write(to: URL(fileURLWithPath: \"model.plist\"))","","\/\/ Load","let data = try Data(contentsOf: URL(fileURLWithPath: \"model.plist\"))","let model = try PropertyListDecoder().decode(MarkovText.self, from: data)"]},{"anchor":"Saving-Only-the-Chain","type":"heading","text":"Saving Only the Chain","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you don’t need overlap checking, save just the chain for a smaller file:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Save only the chain","let chainData = try JSONEncoder().encode(model.chain)","try chainData.write(to: URL(fileURLWithPath: \"chain.json\"))","","\/\/ Load and create MarkovText","let chainData = try Data(contentsOf: URL(fileURLWithPath: \"chain.json\"))","let chain = try JSONDecoder().decode(Chain.self, from: chainData)","let model = MarkovText(chain: chain)"]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without ","type":"text"},{"code":"parsedSentences","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", overlap checking is disabled. Set ","type":"text"},{"code":"testOutput: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when generating, or accept that duplicates may occur.","type":"text"}]}]},{"anchor":"File-Size-Considerations","type":"heading","text":"File Size Considerations","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Model file sizes depend on:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Corpus size"}]},{"text":": Larger corpora produce larger models","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State size"}]},{"text":": Higher state sizes create more unique states","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"retainOriginal"}]},{"text":": Storing parsed sentences increases file size","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Typical file sizes:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Corpus Size","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Approximate JSON Size","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"10 KB text","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"50-100 KB","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"100 KB text","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"500 KB - 1 MB","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1 MB text","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"5-10 MB","type":"text"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To reduce file size:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use binary encoding (PropertyListEncoder)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set ","type":"text"},{"code":"retainOriginal: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if you don’t need overlap checking","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Consider compression (gzip)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Compressing-Saved-Models","type":"heading","text":"Compressing Saved Models","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Compression","","\/\/ Save with compression","let data = try JSONEncoder().encode(model)","let compressed = try (data as NSData).compressed(using: .lzfse)","try compressed.write(to: URL(fileURLWithPath: \"model.json.lzfse\"))","","\/\/ Load with decompression","let compressed = try Data(contentsOf: URL(fileURLWithPath: \"model.json.lzfse\"))","let data = try (compressed as NSData).decompressed(using: .lzfse)","let model = try JSONDecoder().decode(MarkovText.self, from: data as Data)"]},{"anchor":"App-Bundle-Resources","type":"heading","text":"App Bundle Resources","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Include pre-trained models in your app bundle:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["guard let url = Bundle.main.url(","    forResource: \"trained_model\",","    withExtension: \"json\"",") else {","    fatalError(\"Model not found in bundle\")","}","","let data = try Data(contentsOf: url)","var model = try JSONDecoder().decode(MarkovText.self, from: data)","model.compile()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Thread Safety","anchor":"Thread-Safety","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/MarkovText"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" conform to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", making them safe to use across concurrency domains:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let model = try JSONDecoder().decode(MarkovText.self, from: data)","","\/\/ Safe to use from multiple tasks","await withTaskGroup(of: String?.self) { group in","    for _ in 0..<10 {","        group.addTask {","            model.makeSentence()","        }","    }","","    for await sentence in group {","        if let sentence {","            print(sentence)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Important","style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"compile()"},{"type":"text","text":" method mutates the model. Compile before sharing across tasks, or use separate copies."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/MarkovText","doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Advanced Usage","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/CustomizingSentenceSplitting","doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/CombiningModels"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Advanced-Usage"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/PersistingModels","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://ChainLetter/documentation/ChainLetter":{"abstract":[{"text":"A Swift library for building Markov chain text generators.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/docu